to play a game, you'd
have to take that out,

00:10:37.703 --> 00:10:40.872 align:start size:69% position:31%
put another disk in.
And then if it's like,
"Oh, hold on a second.

00:10:40.939 --> 00:10:42.708 align:start size:78% position:22%
I need something back
from this system memory,"

00:10:42.775 --> 00:10:44.343 align:start size:97% position:3%
- you'd have to swap 'em out.
- Yeah.

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:47.913 align:start size:75% position:25%
So it was such a process
because it is loading
everything into the RAM,

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.781 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you obviously don't have
a lot of it to work with.

00:10:49.848 --> 00:10:52.284 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Not a ton of storage.
- And I always will remember,

00:10:52.351 --> 00:10:54.886 align:start size:69% position:31%
