00:13:00.879 --> 00:13:02.147
Humphrey:
<i> So Steve Jobs and the rest
 of their crew,</i>

00:13:02.214 --> 00:13:04.750
<i> they knew they were going to
 have to come up</i>

00:13:04.816 --> 00:13:06.852
<i> with something spectacular
 to put a dent in the universe.</i>

00:13:06.919 --> 00:13:09.187 line:0%
I was the Creative Director
of Apple for,

00:13:09.254 --> 00:13:11.289
like, 17 years altogether.

00:13:11.356 --> 00:13:13.258
There were a number of things
about working with Steve.

00:13:13.325 --> 00:13:16.928
First thing was he was smart.
And I mean, like, really smart.

00:13:16.995 --> 00:13:19.064
<i> But what really set him apart</i>

00:13:19.131 --> 00:13:20.966
<i> was the marketing
 side of him.</i>

00:13:21.033 --> 00:13:22.301
<i> I've worked with
 many big companies.</i>

00:13:22.368 --> 00:13:25.503
<i> I've never met a CEO
 who had that passion</i>

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.939
<i> and talent for marketing.</i>

00:13:28.006 --> 00:13:29.975
He knew that every product
had to tell a story.

00:13:30.042 --> 00:13:32.477
Humphrey:
<i> So Apple created a commercial.</i>

00:13:32.544 --> 00:13:35.247
<i> It was in, I think,
